[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3526195761","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112695#issuecomment-3526195761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112695","id":3526195761,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SLXox","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T07:57:39Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T07:57:39Z","body":"* See also #89853.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I would prefer the name to contain `IMPLICIT_CONVERSION` rather than `IMPLICIT_CAST` (for consistency with `NARROWING_CONVERSION`, and because \"conversion\" is a more general/neutral term, while \"cast\" is associated with more explicit language constructs like the `as` operator, type constructors, etc.).\r\n\r\nWe should also consider whether we'll introduce other `IMPLICIT_CONVERSION_*` warnings (like `IMPLICIT_CONVERSION_CAUSES_COPY`). If so, they should be well-structured and allow users to configure warnings in a meaningful way without cluttering the Project Settings with warnings for every data type.\r\n\r\nWe need to understand in which cases implicit conversions can cause confusion or harm, and in which cases they're more of a stylistic preference that many users won't want to enable (like `String <-> StringName`, `int -> float`).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3526195761/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534072607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112695#issuecomment-3534072607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112695","id":3534072607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Spasf","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T18:38:03Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T18:38:03Z","body":"> Personally, I would prefer the name to contain IMPLICIT_CONVERSION rather than IMPLICIT_CAST (for consistency with NARROWING_CONVERSION, and because \"conversion\" is a more general/neutral term, while \"cast\" is associated with more explicit language constructs like the as operator, type constructors, etc.).\r\n\r\nI agree; I've renamed the warnings to use `IMPLICIT_CONVERSION` instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534072607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534193525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112695#issuecomment-3534193525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112695","id":3534193525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sp4N1","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T19:12:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T19:12:04Z","body":"This many need an extra test, maybe, because `int` to `bool` is **very** common in `if` statements, which you will (or should, if this PR doesn't handle it?) be warned about, too.\r\n\r\nWe also quite literally have a tip in the docs on how to handle all `Error` constants this way:\r\n> Since [OK](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_%40globalscope.html#class-globalscope-constant-ok) has value `0`, and all other error constants are positive integers, it can also be used in boolean checks.\r\n> ```gdscript\r\n> var error = method_that_returns_error()\r\n> if error != OK:\r\n> \tprinterr(\"Failure!\")\r\n> \r\n> # Or, alternatively:\r\n> if error:\r\n> \tprinterr(\"Still failing!\")\r\n> ```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534193525/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]